  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 4. The perturbative expansion, ONE ORDER AT A TIME.\n   Same Baxter residual, same for all four Q. Branch k carries the exponential z_k^(u/h), stripped,\n   so what is expanded is the polynomial part:\n       q_k(u) = P_k(u) + Sum_{n=1..N} eps^n (polynomial of degree dfun[k,n]),\n       tc[i]  = tc0[i] + Sum_{n=1..N} eps^n tcn[i,n],\n       z[j]  -> Exp[I eps psi_j] expanded to order N.\n   At order n the unknowns tcn[.,n] and the order-n polynomial coefficients enter LINEARLY (they\n   multiply order-0 data only); all nonlinear terms involve lower orders, already solved for. So\n   each order is a linear solve. Solving all orders at once instead makes the system quadratic --\n   slow, and it returns spurious branches.\n   Gauge at each order: the coefficient of u^(Mhat_j) in branch k is set to zero for j <= k, which\n   removes the freedom of adding lower untwisted solutions (and fixes the normalisation of P_k).\n   dfun is left as an argument so the degree growth is a hypothesis to be TESTED, not assumed. ---- *)\nClearAll[zser, PertSolve];\nzser[N_] := Table[z[j] -> Normal[Series[Exp[I eps psi[[j]]], {eps, 0, N}]], {j, 4}];\n\nPertSolve[S_, P_, μ_, N_, dfun_] := Module[{u0 = UntwSolve[S, P, μ], dh, x, pf, tcser, R, acc = {}, fr = {}, rep = {}, eqs, unk, gauge, sol},\n   dh = u0[\"Mhat\"];\n   tcser = Table[tc[i] -> u0[\"tc0\"][[i]] + Sum[eps^n tcn[i, n], {n, N}], {i, 5}];\n   pf[k_] := Function[y, Evaluate[qpoly[u0[\"P\"][[k]], y] + Sum[eps^n Sum[pcn[k, j, n] y^j, {j, 0, dfun[k, n]}], {n, N}]]];\n   R = Table[Expand[((BaxRes[S, P, μ][k][pf[k]][x] /. prm) /. zser[N]) /. tcser], {k, 4}];\n   Do[eqs = DeleteCases[Expand[Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[Coefficient[R[[k]], eps, n], x], {k, 4}]] /. acc], 0];\n      unk = Join[Table[tcn[i, n], {i, 5}], Flatten[Table[pcn[k, j, n], {k, 4}, {j, 0, dfun[k, n]}]]];\n      gauge = Flatten[Table[pcn[k, dh[[j]], n], {k, 4}, {j, k}]];\n      sol = Quiet@Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ Join[eqs, gauge], unk];\n      rep = Append[rep, {n, Table[dfun[k, n], {k, 4}], Length[eqs], Length[unk], If[sol === {}, \"INCONSISTENT\", \"ok\"]}];\n      If[sol === {}, Break[]];\n      acc = Join[acc, First[sol]]; fr = Join[fr, Complement[unk, First[sol][[All, 1]]]], {n, N}];\n   <|\"Mhat\" -> dh, \"report\" -> rep, \"sol\" -> acc, \"free\" -> fr, \"orders\" -> Length[rep] - Boole[rep[[-1, -1]] === \"INCONSISTENT\"]|>];\n\n(* order 0 is the untwisted solve; test the degree rule Mhat_k + grow*n for grow = 0,1,2 *)\nGrid[Prepend[Flatten[Table[Prepend[#, Row[{\"grow=\", g}]] & /@ PertSolve[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}, 4, (Mhat[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}][[#1]] + g #2 &)][\"report\"], {g, 0, 2}], 1],\n  {\"variant\", \"order n\", \"degrees\", \"#eqs\", \"#unk\", \"status\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
