     "id": "5c36c7d5-6af1-4057-8b19-da7d5f3f99b5"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 5. The perturbative twisted solver, done properly.\n   The Q-functions stay exponential x polynomial at every twist:  Q_k = z_k^(u/h) q_k,  q_k monic\n   of degree M_k = (S+P) - mu_k, FIXED. Only the COEFFICIENTS are expanded in eps, and they are\n   LAURENT: branch k diverges as eps^(-p_k), p_k = M_k - M_1. The staggered untwisted degrees\n   Mhat_k = M_k + (k-1) of cell 3 are the shadow of exactly this -- expanding Exp[phi u] into\n   polynomials is what raises the degree, so a polynomial ansatz of growing degree is just the\n   exponential written out, and imposing it as an independent ansatz over-constrains the system\n   (cell 4: consistent at eps^1 and eps^2, dead at eps^3). tau stays regular (Taylor from tc0).\n\n   THREE bookkeeping points, each of which produced a spurious \"inconsistent\" before being fixed:\n   - the most divergent orders carry NO equations: those coefficients make a polynomial of degree\n     < M_k, automatically an untwisted solution. The loop starts at -pmax, not at the first order\n     that has equations;\n   - unknowns left undetermined at one order must be CARRIED FORWARD (pend), not dropped;\n   - a tau correction tcn[i,m] multiplies coefficients as divergent as eps^(-pmax), so it first\n     appears in the equations at eps-order m - pmax, NOT at order m. Offering tcn[i,n] at order n\n     is too late by pmax orders. This is the one-order lag of the regular case, generalised. ---- *)\nClearAll[PertQ];\nPertQ[S_, P_, μ_, N_] := Module[{Ms = Mdeg[S, P, μ], u0 = UntwSolve[S, P, μ], pk, pmax, x, qf, tcser, R, acc = {}, pend = {}, rep = {}, eqs, unk, sol, nlo, Ntc},\n   pk = Ms - Min[Ms]; pmax = Max[pk]; Ntc = N + pmax;\n   tcser = Table[tc[i] -> u0[\"tc0\"][[i]] + Sum[eps^n tcn[i, n], {n, Ntc}], {i, 5}];\n   qf[k_] := Function[y, Evaluate[y^Ms[[k]] + Sum[y^j Sum[eps^n cn[k, j, n], {n, -pk[[k]], N}], {j, 0, Ms[[k]] - 1}]]];\n   R = Table[Expand[((BaxRes[S, P, μ][k][qf[k]][x] /. prm) /. zser[Ntc]) /. tcser], {k, 4}];\n   nlo = Min[Table[Min[Exponent[R[[k]], eps, List]], {k, 4}]];\n   Do[eqs = DeleteCases[Expand[Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[Coefficient[R[[k]], eps, n], x], {k, 4}]] /. acc], 0];\n      unk = Join[pend, If[n + pmax >= 1, Table[tcn[i, n + pmax], {i, 5}], {}], Flatten[Table[cn[k, j, n], {k, 4}, {j, 0, Ms[[k]] - 1}]]];\n      unk = DeleteDuplicates[Select[unk, FreeQ[If[acc === {}, {}, acc[[All, 1]]], #] &]];\n      sol = Quiet@Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ eqs, unk];\n      rep = Append[rep, {n, Length[eqs], Length[unk], If[sol === {}, \"INCONSISTENT\", \"ok\"], If[sol === {}, \"-\", Length[Complement[unk, First[sol][[All, 1]]]]]}];\n      If[sol === {}, Break[]];\n      acc = Join[acc, First[sol]]; pend = Complement[unk, First[sol][[All, 1]]], {n, -pmax, N}];\n   <|\"M\" -> Ms, \"pk\" -> pk, \"nlo\" -> nlo, \"report\" -> rep, \"sol\" -> acc, \"pending\" -> pend|>];\n\nWith[{r = PertQ[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}, 4]},\n Column[{Row[{\"M = \", r[\"M\"], \",  divergence orders p_k = \", r[\"pk\"], \",  residual starts at eps^\", r[\"nlo\"]}],\n   Grid[Prepend[r[\"report\"], {\"eps order\", \"#eqs\", \"#unk offered\", \"status\", \"#left free\"}], Frame -> All],\n   Row[{\"still undetermined: \", r[\"pending\"]}]}]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"961320\" data-output-id=\"136\" data-out-n=\"35\" data-sub-idx=\"3\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"5\" data-sub-start=\"33\" data-sub-end=\"36\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[35]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7XCRBYm9ydGVkfQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8056em;vertical-align:-0.0556em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">$Aborted</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[35]= \\text{\\$Aborted}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "f91624cd-4c5f-4b4e-b1b1-ad82151d64c1"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 6. Seeded deformation of the untwisted solutions, with NO exponential assumed.\n   The point missed in cells 4 and 5: BaxRes carries prefactors z[k]^m, i.e. it PRESUPPOSES\n   Q = z_k^(u/h) q_k with q_k a polynomial. A Taylor series of polynomials with growing degree is\n   precisely z^(u/h) written out, so it cannot satisfy the stripped equation -- it satisfies the\n   UNSTRIPPED one, BaxU below, where the twist enters only through tau. That is why the stripped\n   version died at eps^3: for a polynomial of degree M_k + n the subleading residual coefficient is\n   h z_k Prod_{j!=k}(z_k - z_j) (mu_k - S - P + deg), and Prod_{j!=k}(z_k - z_j) = O(eps^3).\n\n   Ansatz: Q = P_k + Sum_{n>=1} eps^n (polynomial of degree deg P_k + n), tau = tc0 + Sum eps^n tcn,\n   solved one order at a time. No 1/eps anywhere.\n   The solution is deliberately NOT unique -- eps^n times any lower untwisted solution may be added.\n   Leftover freedom at each order is simply SET TO ZERO before moving on: that is one legitimate\n   representative, and it keeps every later order LINEAR (carrying the free parameters symbolically\n   makes tcn x qn products and the solve blows up). The count of leftovers is reported. ---- *)\nClearAll[BaxU, SeedSolve];\nBaxU[S_, P_, μ_][Qf_][x_] := Product[ν1[S, P][x - m h], {m, 0, 3}] Qf[x + h] - τ[1][S, P, μ][x] Product[ν1[S, P][x - m h], {m, 1, 3}] Qf[x] + τ[2][S, P, μ][x] Product[ν1[S, P][x - m h], {m, 2, 3}] Qf[x - h] - τ[3][S, P, μ][x] ν1[S, P][x - 3 h] Qf[x - 2 h] + τ[4][S, P, μ][x] Qf[x - 3 h];\n\nSeedSolve[S_, P_, μ_, k_, N_] := Module[{u0 = UntwSolve[S, P, μ], dh, x, Qf, tcser, R, acc = {}, rep = {}, eqs, unk, sol, fr},\n   dh = u0[\"Mhat\"][[k]];\n   tcser = Table[tc[i] -> u0[\"tc0\"][[i]] + Sum[eps^n tcn[i, n], {n, N}], {i, 5}];\n   Qf = Function[y, Evaluate[qpoly[u0[\"P\"][[k]], y] + Sum[eps^n Sum[qn[j, n] y^j, {j, 0, dh + n}], {n, N}]]];\n   R = Expand[((BaxU[S, P, μ][Qf][x] /. prm) /. zser[N]) /. tcser];\n   Do[eqs = DeleteCases[Expand[CoefficientList[Coefficient[R, eps, n], x] /. acc], 0];\n      unk = Join[Table[tcn[i, n], {i, 5}], Table[qn[j, n], {j, 0, dh + n}]];\n      sol = Quiet@Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ eqs, unk];\n      rep = Append[rep, {n, Length[eqs], Length[unk], If[sol === {}, \"INCONSISTENT\", \"ok\"], If[sol === {}, \"-\", Length[Complement[unk, First[sol][[All, 1]]]]]}];\n      If[sol === {}, Break[]];\n      fr = Thread[Complement[unk, First[sol][[All, 1]]] -> 0];\n      acc = Join[Join[acc, First[sol]] /. fr, fr], {n, N}];\n   <|\"seedDeg\" -> dh, \"report\" -> rep, \"sol\" -> acc, \"Qf\" -> Qf|>];\n\nGrid[Prepend[Flatten[Table[Prepend[#, Row[{\"seed P_\", k, \" (deg \", UntwSolve[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}][\"Mhat\"][[k]], \")\"}]] & /@ SeedSolve[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}, k, 4][\"report\"], {k, 4}], 1],\n  {\"seed\", \"order n\", \"#eqs\", \"#unk\", \"status\", \"#free (set to 0)\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
