  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Impose regularity order by order and read off the leading divergence. q1 = q2 = 1 for the vacuum; the same code takes any regular monic q_k. *)\nClearAll[negconds, sol0, lim0];\nnegconds = DeleteCases[Expand[Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[SeriesCoefficient[Q2reg[Function[y, 1], Function[y, 1], 2], {eps, 0, n}], u], {n, -3, -1}]]], 0];\nsol0 = Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ negconds, Flatten[Table[{av[n], bv[n]}, {n, -3, -1}]]];\nlim0 = Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[Q2reg[Function[y, 1], Function[y, 1], 2], {eps, 0, 0}] /. First[sol0]];\n{\"conditions from the negative orders\" -> negconds, \"solved\" -> First[sol0], \"eps^0 limit\" -> lim0, \"degree of the limit in u\" -> Exponent[lim0, u]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
