  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* k = 3. Q3reg = a1 Exp[phi1 u] q1 + a2 Exp[phi2 u] q2 + a3 Exp[phi3 u] q3, with q1 = q2 = 1 and q3 monic of degree M_3 = 2 and REGULAR in eps (that assumption is what the case tests). The a_i are Laurent. Impose that no negative power of eps survives and read off the leading divergence and the degree of the eps^0 limit, which should be Mhat_3 = 4. *)\nClearAll[q3f, Q3reg, neg3, sol3, lim3];\nq3f[y_] := y^2 + (c11 + eps c12) y + (c01 + eps c02);\nQ3reg[nord_] := Normal[Series[Sum[eps^n a1v[n], {n, -3, 2}] Exp[I eps psi[[1]] u] + Sum[eps^n a2v[n], {n, -3, 2}] Exp[I eps psi[[2]] u] + Sum[eps^n a3v[n], {n, -3, 2}] Exp[I eps psi[[3]] u] q3f[u], {eps, 0, nord}]];\nneg3 = DeleteCases[Expand[Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[SeriesCoefficient[Q3reg[2], {eps, 0, n}], u], {n, -3, -1}]]], 0];\nsol3 = Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ neg3, Flatten[Table[{a1v[n], a2v[n], a3v[n]}, {n, -3, -1}]]];\nlim3 = Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[Q3reg[2], {eps, 0, 0}] /. First[sol3]];\n{\"#conditions\" -> Length[neg3], \"solved\" -> First[sol3], \"eps^0 limit\" -> lim3, \"degree of limit\" -> Exponent[lim3, u]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div>",
