      {
       "data": "Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \"solve\" variables.",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      },
      {
       "data": "{\n\t\"name\": \"WolframKernelMessage\",\n\t\"message\": \"Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \\\"solve\\\" variables.\",\n\t\"stack\": \"\"\n}",
       "mime": "application/vnd.code.notebook.error"
      }
     ],
     "id": "f5385044-8c40-4b1c-85c0-c4b624a78173"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Previous cell: with q3 REGULAR the limit has degree 2 = M_3, not Mhat_3 = 4 -- so a monic q_3 cannot be regular. Now let q3's own coefficients be Laurent, normalise a3 = 1, and find the pole order they need and the degree they then reach. *)\nClearAll[q3L, Q3L, neg3L, sol3L, lim3L];\nq3L[y_] := y^2 + Sum[eps^n c1v[n], {n, -3, 1}] y + Sum[eps^n c0v[n], {n, -3, 1}];\nQ3L[nord_] := Normal[Series[Sum[eps^n a1v[n], {n, -3, 2}] Exp[I eps psi[[1]] u] + Sum[eps^n a2v[n], {n, -3, 2}] Exp[I eps psi[[2]] u] + Exp[I eps psi[[3]] u] q3L[u], {eps, 0, nord}]];\nneg3L = DeleteCases[Expand[Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[SeriesCoefficient[Q3L[2], {eps, 0, n}], u], {n, -3, -1}]]], 0];\nsol3L = Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ neg3L, Flatten[Table[{a1v[n], a2v[n], c1v[n], c0v[n]}, {n, -3, -1}]]];\nlim3L = Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[Q3L[2], {eps, 0, 0}] /. First[sol3L]];\n{\"#conditions\" -> Length[neg3L], \"solved\" -> First[sol3L], \"eps^0 limit\" -> lim3L, \"degree of limit\" -> Exponent[lim3L, u]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
