   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* How far regularity alone gets us at k = 3. Scan the deepest pole allowed (pmin) against the degree of the eps^0 limit. q3 = c2 u^2 + c1 u + c0 with ALL coefficients Laurent (dropping monic, since a3 q3 is one object), a1 and a2 Laurent. Conclusion: unlike k = 2, regularity does NOT fix the pole depth -- the reachable degree simply follows how deep the poles are allowed to go, and Mhat_3 = 4 needs eps^-4. So for k >= 3 the divergence order has to come from the Baxter equation, not from regularity of the combination. *)\nClearAll[degFree];\ndegFree[pmin_] := Module[{q3x, Q3x, negx, solx, limx, unk}, q3x[y_] := Sum[y^i Sum[eps^n cv[i, n], {n, pmin, 1}], {i, 0, 2}]; Q3x[nord_] := Normal[Series[Sum[eps^n a1v[n], {n, pmin, 2}] Exp[I eps psi[[1]] u] + Sum[eps^n a2v[n], {n, pmin, 2}] Exp[I eps psi[[2]] u] + Exp[I eps psi[[3]] u] q3x[u], {eps, 0, nord}]]; negx = DeleteCases[Expand[Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[SeriesCoefficient[Q3x[2], {eps, 0, n}], u], {n, pmin, -1}]]], 0]; unk = Flatten[Table[{a1v[n], a2v[n], cv[0, n], cv[1, n], cv[2, n]}, {n, pmin, -1}]]; solx = Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ negx, unk]; limx = Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[Q3x[2], {eps, 0, 0}] /. First[solx]]; {pmin, Exponent[limx, u], Length[Complement[unk, First[solx][[All, 1]]]]}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[degFree[p], {p, {-1, -2, -3, -4}}], {\"deepest pole eps^pmin\", \"degree of eps^0 limit\", \"#free\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<details class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">4 warnings</summary><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">General::stop: Further output of Solve::svars will be suppressed during this calculation.</div></details>",
