  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* The real test: a state where q_2 is not trivial. mu = {2,1,1,0} gives M = {0,1,1,2}, so q_1 = 1 but q_2 is monic of degree 1 with Laurent coefficients starting at eps^-(M_2-M_1) = eps^-1. Same two branches only. *)\nSetState[1, 1, {2, 1, 1, 0}];\nWith[{r = pushQ12[1, 1, {2, 1, 1, 0}, 6]}, Column[{Row[{\"mu = {2,1,1,0}, M = \", r[\"M\"], \", so q_2 diverges as 1/eps\"}], Grid[Prepend[r[\"report\"], {\"order n\", \"#eqs\", \"#unk\", \"status\", \"#free\"}], Frame -> All]}]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
