   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Does keeping only Q1 and Q2 fix all of tau? YES, with a one-order lag: pushing to eps^N fixes every tc completely at orders 1..N-1, and only the top order N keeps free directions. The per-order \"#free\" in the table above counts the CURRENT order's leftovers, which the next order then removes -- the back-substitution acc -> Join[acc /. new, new] is what propagates that. NB pushQ12 reads S, P, mu through Bax, so call SetState for the SAME state first. *)\nSetState[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}];\nrv = pushQ12[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}, 8];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[With[{v = Table[tcn[i, m] /. rv[\"sol\"], {i, 5}]}, {m, Count[v, _?(FreeQ[#, _tcn] &)], DeleteDuplicates[Cases[v, _tcn, Infinity]]}], {m, 8}], {\"order m\", \"#tc fully fixed (of 5)\", \"remaining free\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
